[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_script")
entry_name = "Lua Item Discovery"
description = "Automatica sees the game's real item catalogue. list_items() returns a sorted list of every item name.

print(type(list_items))      -- function
local items = list_items()   -- list of names
print(#items > 0)            -- true

Use an exact name from that list with withdraw() to pull items from the nearest chest into the robot's build palette:

withdraw(\"Wood\", 10)

The same names work with put_input(\"Wood\", 10) for station automation. Item names are case-insensitive in the game API, but exact names are easier to read."
keyword = "list_items"
language = "lua"
category = "Medium"
